  "question": {
    "text": "Let the foot of perpendicular from the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> on the plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>&#8484;</mi></math> is a point on plane&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> such that the area of the triangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>N</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>&#946;</mi></math> is equal to _____________",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "7",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,</p><p>The foot of perpendicular from the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> on the plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi></math></p><p>So, by foot of perpendicular formula we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>And&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>&#8484;</mi></math> is a point on plane&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> such that the area of the triangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>N</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math>,</p><p>So putting the value of point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;in plane we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#946;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math></p><p>And given area of triangle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>N</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math>, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">&#215;</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>N</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">&#215;</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>6</mn><msqrt><mn>6</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>18</mn><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mtext>as</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mtext>as&#160;</mtext><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>So, &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></math></p></blockquote>",
